# THE GALLERY DRAWS ON PUBLISHER FIGURES, and what it writes is a crop of one.
# `png/verify.py` puts G1-G4 back into the tree every time it runs, and a
# `git add -A` after that run is exactly how ten rasters and eleven PNGs came to
# be tracked in a public repository in the first place. The pictures are
# deliverables, not records: run the gallery, look at them, do not commit them.
